WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.100
Oh, what's this?

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:12.900
Gyokuran?!

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.520
H-H-Hey! Hey!

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.320
Calm down, Yaichiro.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.540
What a strange hole.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.690
Wh-Wh-Wh-What is this?!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.560
Where are we?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.830
This is Father's shogi room.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.730
Delicious...

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.650
curry!

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.840
So it was inside the shogi board.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:04.750
It wasn't this dirty when we were kids.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:08.950
What's the tea-kettle engine
doing in the shogi room?

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.190
What do you think is behind this door?

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:17.800
I'm really curious to know...

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.940
Why does it smell so strongly of curry?

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.640
You stupid furballs.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.270
What are you doing?

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:37.170
"Nasebanaru" to hito wa yuuga

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:37.170
People say, "Where there's 
a will, there's a way"

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.730
Narugamama naseba ii

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.730
But things can just be how they'll be

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.200
Nagareru kawa ukabu kobune

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:53.200
A small boat floats along the river

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.130
Doko ni yukuno darouka

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.130
I wonder where it's going

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.320
Ikisaki nado yosou dekinu

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.320
I can't even guess its destination

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.600
Sorega omoshiroki koto

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.600
But that's why it's so fun

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:15.730
Kokorozashi wa takaku mokuhyou wa hikuku

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:15.730
My intentions are high, but my goals are low

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:20.740
Aho wo mazerya kekka

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:20.740
When foolishness gets mixed in

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:28.410
Yukai ni nareru

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:28.410
Everything will be merry

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:34.560
Narugamama ni sawagu mama ni

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:34.560
As things will be, as chaotic as they will be

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.550
Toraburu suramo nenryou sa

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.550
Even troubles become fuel

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:43.730
Namikaze tatanai jinsei wa

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:43.730
A life lived without any strife

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:48.230
Chotto bakkari tsumaranai

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:48.230
Can be a bit boring

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.960
Okiraku ni gokuraku ni

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.960
Carefree and blissfully

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.510
Kaze ni makasete ikou

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.510
Let's let the wind lead us

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.950
Kyou mo bakashite ikou

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.950
Let's go trick everyone again today

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.950
<b>Episode Five
 Daimonji Luxury Liner Battle Continued</b>

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.550
Well, I'll be going now.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.640
Thanks, Yasaburo-chan.

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.120
It was nothing.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.730
Oh, yeah. The Gozan Farewell Bonfire
is coming up soon.

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:18.470
You should come to our luxury liner, too.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.710
I will definitely come by.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.260
<b>Demachi-bashi Bridge</b>

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.440
See you.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:28.220
Why do you always have to meddle?

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.280
What?

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.350
I do something nice for you,
and that's your attitude?

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:36.900
We don't have a ship
for the Gozan Farewell Bonfire.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:37.720
What?

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:41.720
I thought you were going to borrow
an envoy ship from the tanuki in Nara.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.140
That fell through.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.740
I see.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:51.460
So the Nara tanuki said that
you couldn't borrow the ship.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.430
Yeah.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.000
That's not all.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:59.460
They told me they wouldn't be done
with repairs from the damages last year,

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.270
but let the Ebisugawas borrow it.

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.010
Curse that Kinkaku and Ginkaku.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.760
They let their money speak for them.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.440
Someone must have given
those fools some intelligence.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:14.400
But I can't say that I can
see Kaisei helping them.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:18.550
The one pulling the strings has to be Soun.

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:21.310
It's been six months since he disappeared.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.440
It's about time for him to get bored

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:26.410
with visiting hot springs
and start meddling again.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.530
What about the Farewell Bonfire?

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.400
Hm...

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.540
Just leave it to me.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.420
Sensei,

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:46.840
may I borrow the tea-kettle
engine for a while?

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.850
What are you going to use it for?

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:54.140
All it does is drink wine
and float up into the air.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.920
You do know that we tanuki

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:00.210
fly up into the night sky to enjoy
the Gozan Farewell Bonfire, right?

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:03.320
Ah, so it's that time of year again.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.780
I humbly ask that you let us borrow it.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:07.130
Very well.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:09.940
But on one condition.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.040
Anything you ask.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.440
Do not invite me to go
to see the farewell bonfire.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.960
I will not go.

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:21.110
But the festivities won't start
unless you show up, Sensei.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:25.040
I don't have free time to spend
on tanuki festivities.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:27.590
By the way, Yasaburo.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:30.770
I heard that you were present

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:33.460
when that fool got violent with Benten.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:38.520
What are you doing,
sneaking off to his place?

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:40.520
Explain yourself.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.130
It was a rather humble gift,

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:45.470
but we gave the Nidaime
a housewarming gift.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.160
How many times must I tell you?

00:05:48.350 --> 00:05:51.420
He is not my son, he's not a tengu,

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.740
and he's not the Nidaime.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:56.310
Benten will inherit the legacy
of Nyoigatake Yakushibo.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:58.190
That's what I've decided.

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.330
I've made my decision!

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.290
Sensei,

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:05.130
I don't think you need
to be in such a hurry, do you?

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.170
It's not as though you're
retiring today or tomorrow.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:09.240
Shut up!

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:13.470
You are never to call him the Nidaime again.

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.470
Well, that's quite troublesome.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:18.110
What should I call him, then?

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.880
You might as well call him
the obscene gentleman.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.690
Uh...

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.650
Go buy me some cotton swabs!

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.640
If I don't have any cotton swabs,

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:28.650
my ears will be all itchy,
and I'll let some whirlwinds fly.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.450
Yes, yes, right away.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:45.250
There.

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:48.880
Uh...

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.820
Um...

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.470
Let's start out as friends.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:55.940
But we're already friends.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:00.550
P-P-Please go out with me.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.660
To where?

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.380
That's not what I mean.

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:05.360
Please stop beating around the bush.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.440
Please just say, "I love you." Right now.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.650
Look me right in the eyes,

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.870
and hurry up and say it.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.450
Why are you hesitating?

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:19.060
Come on! Come on! Come on! Come on!

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.210
Don't go overboard!

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.210
Ow...

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.330
What was that for?

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.800
After I offered to...

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.320
We're all ready!

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:36.640
Everyone, please take your seats.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:39.600
This ship will be taking off momentarily.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:44.520
All aboard!

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.450
Make sure you drive safely!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.280
Tanuki don't know
the first thing about flying!

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.670
How dare you steer so violently

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:02.660
when someone as important
as I am is onboard!

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.150
Bing.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:10.240
We have now reached cruising altitude.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:13.540
I told you to drive this thing safely!

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:17.970
Well, Yajiro-niichan went really fast.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.040
Sorry.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.020
I got a bit ahead of myself.

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:22.500
Oh, dear.

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:25.280
The soup spilled everywhere.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:29.460
But the chirashizushi was messy
to begin with, so it should be fine.

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:35.450
There you are, sir.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:40.590
Yaichiro, are you not going
to transform into Hotei?

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.450
I'm going to pass tonight.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:45.880
Well, aren't you acting rather smugly.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:50.310
Gyokuran's here today,
so my brother is trying to impress.

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:51.600
Oho...

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.420
So you furballs are thinking
about getting married.

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:58.300
Well, there's no harm in that.
Go on, stare each other down!

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.500
Sensei, we aren't in a sumo match.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:04.140
Yaichiro-san is looking rather troubled.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:07.230
And why is a furball trying to act so tough?

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:09.450
Did you think you could
hide your affections

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.480
from someone as experienced as myself?

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.980
Long ago, I'd see Soichiro and Tousen

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:20.490
standing at the threshold of love
without walking across it,

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:23.080
and it irritated me greatly.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.300
Right.

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:30.250
And that's when you trapped Soichiro-san
and me inside that shogi room,

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:33.650
and said, "Either get closer
or knock it off.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:38.680
I'm not letting you two out
until you've settled this once and for all."

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.480
In the end, they decided to get closer,

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.800
and you runts were born.
You should be thankful.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.030
I had no idea something like that happened.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:53.500
Furballs are truly troublesome creatures.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.110
If you love her, just say so.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:08.900
I love you.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:11.580
I love you.

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:18.870
Sensei, you truly are on another level.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.090
Of course.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.800
I am a great man.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:24.900
Hmph.

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:27.930
Run along and be happy now.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.920
This turned into a wonderful night.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.380
A fun thing is a good thing.

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.420
It's too bad you're stuck
in that form right now.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:47.410
Well, it's not lonely.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.920
My belly is warming up
from everyone's merriment.

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:55.670
Living as a frog at the bottom of a well

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:58.920
means that your belly is always getting cold.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.660
A fun thing is a good thing.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:03.390
Oh?

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.050
I feel like something just got on my back.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.950
<b>Site of Benten's Fall</b>

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:26.850
The breeze is so cool, Yasaburo.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:29.410
You should come join me.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:33.830
What's the Nidaime's chaise doing here?

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.580
I thought I would gaze at the night scenery

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:38.840
as I lazed around on this lovely chaise.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:41.540
Isn't it a bad idea to take something

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.230
from the Nidaime without permission?

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:45.320
Oh, you're such a scaredy-cat.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:46.930
Well, of course I'm scared!

00:11:47.420 --> 00:11:51.220
I wonder what the problem
at hand right now is.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:54.400
Whether I feel comfortable or not, right?

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.630
Say, Yasaburo.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:00.580
Who do you like more, me or the Nidaime?

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:03.640
I respect you both as tengu.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:06.410
Tanuki are meant to respect tengu.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.870
I hate ambiguous answers like that.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:13.120
Say that again,
and I'll put you into a hot pot.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:17.110
You must be rather angry
at the Nidaime, Benten-sama.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:17.860
Oh?

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.380
But I'm having fun.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:22.840
Everything is fun to me.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.220
Well, if it isn't Benten!

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:27.220
Stay right there. I'll come to you.

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:31.020
Look over there, Yasaburo.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:32.930
Your friends have arrived.

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:52.250
Now, then, my dear fellows
of the Shimogamo clan...

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:56.260
As an English gentleman,
I ask you to allow me a word.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:59.960
Isn't that a train,
rather than a luxury liner?

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.340
I'm sure that's just
Yajiro transformed, Nii-san.

00:13:03.340 --> 00:13:07.740
Aha. In that case,
it wouldn't even be a train.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.970
If we were you, we'd be too ashamed
to even fly these skies.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:14.160
Well, they don't know any shame.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.460
They couldn't get
a luxury liner for the bonfire

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:18.960
so they're sipping tea inside a trick train.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:24.180
Proper tanuki would be so ashamed
that the fur on their behinds would fall out.

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:24.680
Ahem!

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:27.780
Behold how magnificent
our ship is in comparison!

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:30.900
Behold our ingenious taste!

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:36.290
<b>English Gentleman</b>

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:35.430
Completely prepared, <i>tout va bien</i>!

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:37.750
Capable tanuki know what's up!

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.250
Completely prepared, <i>tout va bien</i>!

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.140
Well, what do you think?

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:44.710
Upset? Just try and say something back!

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.130
Shut up, Kinkaku!

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:49.120
That was the ship we were going to borrow.

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.890
You played dirty to get it.

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.710
Are you trying to say
that we took it from you?

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:55.250
Come now, Yasaburo.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.860
Stop with your pathetic excuses.

00:13:57.860 --> 00:13:59.060
Stop.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.360
Just stop.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:04.610
Being someone as responsible as I am,
I just went up to the Nanto elders and said,

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:08.860
"Heya! It's me, Kinkaku!

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:12.870
Just hook me up
with whatever again this year!"

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:18.030
Isn't giving them a proper greeting
the most obvious thing to do?

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:20.080
My brother's very proper.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.880
He's different from an
unsophisticated tanuki like you!

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:23.950
Yes, indeed.

00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.590
After all, I am an English gentleman.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:29.090
And along with a greeting,

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.600
it's common courtesy
to bring a gift, isn't it?

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:35.280
And is there a lovelier gift
than our Trick Denki Bran

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.610
that's filled with our heart and soul?

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.350
I don't believe there is.

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:42.780
Which means the Nanto elders
would want to repay us

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:47.110
for our kindness with a lovely gift, as well.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.530
Precisely, Nii-san!

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:52.540
Not to mention our luxury liner
was shot down last year.

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:53.490
Yes, yes.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:57.120
And who shot it down?

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.610
Why, it was you, Yasaburo!

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:04.210
Your ungentlemanly ways
cause us so much trouble.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:05.590
Even Kaisei said,

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:09.690
"Yasaburo and the others are so violent that
I don't want to ride in the luxury liner,"

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:12.820
and holed up in the Trick Denki Bran factory.

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:14.670
She even said something as inhumane as,

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:17.060
"I'm better off working."

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:20.590
Ah, my poor little eccentric sister.

00:15:20.590 --> 00:15:23.440
Kinkaku, Ginkaku, that's enough!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:24.200
Oh?

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.050
Why's Gyokuran riding with you?

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.720
I heard every single word you said,

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:30.740
and each and every one was extremely rude!

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.920
Apologize right now!

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:36.330
When you were little furballs,
you were cute sometimes!

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:40.350
What on Earth did you eat to become
the annoying little fools you've become?

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:43.340
What's the point of fools
who aren't the least bit cute?!

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:45.980
My, how rude!

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.300
We're deeply hurt.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.950
Oh, you're hurt?

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:52.640
If those words stung you,
you might still have hope.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:54.530
Now, apologize!

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.140
Or else, I'm telling Kaisei-chan on you.

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:00.120
I want to say something back!

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.420
But we can't!

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:02.870
I <i>so</i> want to say something back!

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.100
But we can't!

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:07.050
What the heck? You shogi nut!

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:09.750
Why don't you just play shogi
at Nanzenji forever?

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.780
What did you just say?!

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.530
You're going to insult Gyokuran now, too?

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.950
That's unforgivable!

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.380
Nii-san! Get behind him!

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:24.620
Leave it to me!

00:16:25.030 --> 00:16:27.420
Two against one is bad for us.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.670
Start firing!

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.550
Ow, ow!

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:42.390
Nii-san!

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:48.740
Ow!

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.990
I think my butt's on fire!

00:16:55.350 --> 00:16:56.870
Nii-san, land!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.370
Where am I supposed to land?

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.490
On the Ebisugawa ship, of course!

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.130
Ow, ow! Ow!

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:08.960
Yashiro!

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:09.930
Right!

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:11.690
This way, this way!

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:12.760
Fire! Fire!

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:39.070
Apparently, tanuki

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:42.210
are truly irredeemable fools.

00:17:43.990 --> 00:17:46.190
Are you all right, Nii-san?

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:48.330
Yeah. Good grief.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.090
Thank goodness everyone's safe.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:57.780
What an awful sight.

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:01.300
Tanuki truly never learn.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.330
Of course the furballs never learn.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:15.490
I thought it was a tengu's job
to educate the tanuki.

00:18:19.230 --> 00:18:21.450
Who is that woman?

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:24.180
She is my very capable apprentice.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.880
Unlike you, she actually has a spine.

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:30.650
A thieving woman?
A mighty fine apprentice indeed.

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:35.340
I'm sure it must be rather delightful
needing others in order to fly.

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:38.860
You're free to continue
to grow old and unslightly,

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.340
but you should educate that woman

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:44.810
and at least have her stay out of my sight.

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:47.770
Is that all you have to say?

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:49.850
This isn't good!

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.120
L-Let go!

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.120
H-Hey!

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:52.150
Sensei!

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:54.960
If you use your fan here,

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:57.260
we're all going to get blown away!

00:18:57.840 --> 00:19:00.140
This is between us tengu.

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:03.030
Tanuki should stay out of tengu disputes.

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:06.840
But enjoying the Farewell Bonfire
is a festival for us tanuki,

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:09.540
and this was a tanuki dispute to begin with!

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.520
Please don't forget that!

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:14.630
Tengu getting involved
in a tanuki dispute is just strange!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.330
It's all right, Yasaburo.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:24.730
Master, would you allow me to handle this?

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:26.730
Very well.

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:28.120
Go ahead.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:41.220
When we met in London,
the sky was rather stormy.

00:19:42.440 --> 00:19:45.030
I've disliked you

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:47.490
ever since that day.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.760
Well, my little furballs...

00:20:17.760 --> 00:20:19.830
If you'll excuse me, I'll be taking my leave.

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:32.010
Do you know where Benten fell, Yasaburo?

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:33.300
Yes.

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:36.440
We must go fetch her.

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:38.490
Come with me.

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:39.930
As you wish.

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.340
Sensei...

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:25.080
Are you frustrated?

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.340
I am.

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:29.850
I see.

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.510
I imagine you are.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:37.190
But even tengu fall sometimes.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:42.330
If you're frustrated, grow stronger.

00:21:44.060 --> 00:21:48.450
<i>The moment Benten charged toward the Nidaime,</i>

00:21:49.190 --> 00:21:53.410
<i>her expression filled my chest
with an indescribable sorrow.</i>

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:57.620
<i>I knew that Benten would lose
to the Nidaime...</i>

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:09.230
Tsuki wo medetewa toki ni wa nusunde

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:09.230
While gazing lovingly at the 
moon, at times, she steals it

00:22:09.230 --> 00:22:14.060
Kimagure na kanojo wa ah

00:22:09.230 --> 00:22:14.060
Whimsical as she may be, ah

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:18.530
Kawabe de hitori hoho ni namida

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:18.530
As she stands by the riverside 
alone, secretly her tears

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:22.880
Utsukushiku tayutau

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:22.880
Quiver beautifully upon her cheeks

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:34.660
Boku no te tori nagara 
kokoro wa dokoka ni ukabu

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:34.660
She takes my hand, as her 
heart floats away somewhere

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:39.170
Kasaneta te ni wa mada nukumori

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:39.170
I still feel that warmth from her held hand

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:43.540
Setsunai yume no sono ato saki

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:43.540
Somewhere beyond this sentimental dream

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:53.170
Demo kimi no me wa harukana 
mirai wo miteitane

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:53.170
But you were already looking 
far into the future

00:22:53.170 --> 00:22:57.840
Zutto zutto oikaketayo

00:22:53.170 --> 00:22:57.840
I always chased after you

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:02.190
Kimi ga kizutsuku toki mo

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:02.190
Even when you were hurt

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:11.560
Sotto mabuta ni yakitsuita kimi no sugata ni

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:11.560
The vision of you that's 
softly imprinted on my eyes

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:16.480
Ima mata tooku e to ah

00:23:11.560 --> 00:23:16.480
Once again, you fly far away, ah

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:28.920
Tondeiku kimi wa hora Kanata no hito

00:23:16.480 --> 00:23:28.920
You are a person far beyond

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:34.490
An outdoor bath and coffee milk
make such a miraculous combination.

00:23:34.490 --> 00:23:35.930
How lovely.

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:39.390
By the way, why am I here?

00:23:37.680 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Episode Six
 Arima Hell</b>
